13) WHY STORE SIBLINGS IS POWERFUL
===============================================================================

Benefits:
1) no data loss
2) preserves user intent
3) application-specific merge possible
4) causality preserved
5) safer under partitions
6) better than timestamp overwrites

Real systems:
shopping carts
sets
counters
collaborative edits
offline sync

===============================================================================
14) TRADEOFFS — VERY IMPORTANT FOR HLD
===============================================================================

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- no lost updates
- causality aware
- partition tolerant
- merge later possible
- perfect for eventual consistency
- user intent safe

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- storage overhead
- read complexity badh jati hai
- app ko merge logic likhna padta hai
- sibling explosion ho sakta hai
- counters ke liye read expensive if many siblings
- metadata (vector clock) large ho sakta hai

===============================================================================
15) SIBLING EXPLOSION PROBLEM
===============================================================================

Suppose 100 replicas partition mein chale gaye.
Sabne same key update kar diya.

Now:
100 siblings.

Read pe:
- fetch all
- merge all
- write resolved copy

Ye expensive hai.

Solutions:
- bounded vector clocks
- background compaction
- semantic merge
- CRDT counters
- actor partitioning
- leader-per-key

===============================================================================
16) BEST MERGE STRATEGIES BY DATA TYPE
===============================================================================

Counter:
sum all siblings

Shopping cart:
set union

Profile bio:
manual conflict resolution

Document:
OT / CRDT merge

Bank balance:
NEVER sibling merge blindly
needs transactional ledger

Interview gold:
Conflict resolution must be domain semantic, not storage semantic.

===============================================================================
17) WHY VERSION VECTORS > TIMESTAMPS
===============================================================================

Timestamp issue:
clock skew

Node A clock ahead by 10 sec
Node B actual later write but lower timestamp

Wrong overwrite ho jayega.

Vector clocks:
- causality safe
- detects concurrency
- no wall clock dependency

Tradeoff:
metadata bigger

