22) FAANG LEVEL FINAL TAKEAWAY
===============================================================================

The deepest lesson:

In distributed systems,
the database often cannot decide the correct business truth.

Its job is:
preserve causality + preserve all possible truths.

Application’s job is:
merge those truths semantically.

This separation of:
storage conflict detection
vs
domain conflict resolution

is what senior distributed system design is all about.

If you can explain:
distributed counter → lost update → vector clocks →
concurrency detection → sibling storage → semantic merge →
tradeoffs

you are absolutely ready for top HLD interviews.

